    {
      "id": "pTXBv_9H1tfumudMHNZsF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7529.907018,
      "y": -8246.71539170788,
      "width": 98.29695129394531,
      "height": 158.1539633309676,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#099268",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bjcOM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 726810947,
      "version": 2483,
      "versionNonce": 1161080380,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760965817787,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Clicking and dragging between two points\n(arrow origin and destination) draws AND\n\"completes\" the arrow in a single action. \n\nSingle clicks without moving the mouse\nwill add \"points\" to the arrow's path.\nThis will allow arrows that zigzag (in the\ncase of Straight arrows) or arrows that\nwind and turn, with multiple curves (in\nthe case of Curved Arrows.\n\nArrows can be drawn free-floating, but\nwork best when attached to\nshapes/objects, as the objects act like\nanchors, allowing you to move things\naround as the arrows adjust accordingly.\n\n\n--------------------------\n\nThere are three boxes below this text.\nTry moving each one around and see how\nthe different arrows interact.\n(arrows can get a little glitchy\nsometimes, so it's okay if anything acts\nweird!",
      "fontSize": 4.866275794799003,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "2L7NcT9Wdj_gI6PmHMxNM",
      "originalText": "Clicking and dragging between two points (arrow origin and destination) draws AND \"completes\" the arrow in a single action. \n\nSingle clicks without moving the mouse will add \"points\" to the arrow's path. This will allow arrows that zigzag (in the case of Straight arrows) or arrows that wind and turn, with multiple curves (in the case of Curved Arrows.\n\nArrows can be drawn free-floating, but work best when attached to shapes/objects, as the objects act like anchors, allowing you to move things around as the arrows adjust accordingly.\n\n\n--------------------------\n\nThere are three boxes below this text. Try moving each one around and see how the different arrows interact.\n(arrows can get a little glitchy sometimes, so it's okay if anything acts weird!",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
